OL,3,GNEWSAAsian hornets 'established'
OL,4,Adespite sightings drop
OL,5,
OL,6,FFewer yellow-legged hornets have been
OL,7,Frecorded this year than in 2025, but
OL,8,Fthe discovery of nests across a wider
OL,9,Farea has raised concerns from a local
OL,10,Fgroup that the species is becoming
OL,11,Festablished in the South East.
OL,13,FAlso known as the Asian hornet, it is
OL,14,Fan "invasive, non-native species" which
OL,15,Fhas been sighted in the region
OL,16,Fpreviously.
OL,18,FAsian hornets feed on insects and are a
OL,19,Fthreat to bees, because they like to
OL,20,Ffeed bee grubs and dismembered adult
OL,21,Fbee thoraxes to their young, beekeepers
OL,22,Fsay.
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
